## Strategy
You are doing great! Moving from sorting simple integers to sorting an array of structs is a fantastic step forward. The logic remains exactly the same as the **Bubble Sort** we saw in `demo_problem_sort.c`. 

The secret is that instead of comparing two integers like `arr[j] > arr[j + 1]`, you simply compare the specific **field** inside your structs. If you have an array of `Student` structs, you just access the field using the dot operator (e.g., `students[j].grade`). When you need to swap the elements, you swap the **entire struct** at once, not just the individual field!

## Visual Logic
```mermaid
