    A["Start Loop"] --> B["Is current.field > next.field?"]
    B -- Yes --> C["Create temp struct"]
    C --> D["Swap entire structs: arrj = arrj+1"]
    D --> E["Finish Swap"]
    B -- No --> F["Move to next pair"]
    E --> F
    F --> G["End of array?"]
    G -- No --> B
    G -- Yes --> H["Sorted!"]
```

## Implementation Plan
1. **Identify the Field**: Determine which struct member you want to sort by (e.g., `score`).
2. **Use a Temporary Struct**: When swapping, create a temporary variable of the **same struct type** to hold the data while you move the elements around.
3. **Apply Bubble Sort**: Use the nested loop structure from `demo_problem_sort.c`, but replace the integer comparison with your struct field comparison.

```c
// Example: Sorting an array of 'Student' structs by 'score'
for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
        // Compare the specific field
        if (students[j].score > students[j + 1].score) {
            // Swap the entire struct
            Student temp = students[j];
            students[j] = students[j + 1];
            students[j + 1] = temp;
        }
    }
}
```

