    B --> C["SIGINT Signal Sent"]
    C --> D["Programs Signal Handler"]
    D --> E["Cleanup Code: Close files/save data"]
    E --> F["Program exits gracefully"]
```

## Example from Class
While `SIGINT` is not in your provided notes, it is typically implemented using the `signal.h` library. You would define a function to handle the interrupt and then register it in your `main` function:

```c
#include <signal.h>
#include <stdio.h>

void handle_sigint(int sig) {
    printf("\nCaught the signal! Cleaning up...\n");
}

int main() {
    signal(SIGINT, handle_sigint);
    // Program logic goes here
    return 0;
}
```

